  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: ae309fc9b93c4434b888290b1d747f9a, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::TeacherInteraction
  playerMovement: {fileID: 19591689}
  teacherName: Dreyfus
  dialoguePopUp: {fileID: 1256853252}
  dialogueManager: {fileID: 1682790333}
  spellSelectionScreen: {fileID: 0}
  battleScreen: {fileID: 0}
  element: 
  totalNumOfElementSpells: 0
  battleCanvas: {fileID: 972287457}
  eventSystem: {fileID: 0}
  initalLines:
  - Do you know the relationship between numbers and the world?
  - Numbers are formulaic, each equation forming an answer, and each equation can
    be broken into its smaller parts.
  - The same can be said for magic, each spell weaved precisely. If you break apart
    a spell you can analyze its parts, and by further understanding your magic, you
    can become more powerful.
  - "Try to put it into practice and break apart Taylor\u2019s magic over there."
  afterPuzzleLines:
  - Breaking a problem into smaller pieces always helps analyze the greater whole.
  - "I\u2019ll give you a new problem to solve."
  afterBattleLines:
  - You really broke down that problem well.
  - "It seems you\u2019ve picked up on the mathematical side of math."
  afterSpellLines:
  - "Smaller tasks are more manageable than larger ones, but don\u2019t forget the
    bigger picture. Make sure you can put together what you learn."
